  "Question": "Karl bought five folders from Pay-A-Lot at a cost of \\(\\$2.50\\) each. Pay-A-Lot had a \\(20\\%\\)-off sale the following day. How much could Karl have saved on the purchase by waiting a day?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\$ 1.00\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\$ 2.00\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\$ 2.50\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\$ 2.75\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\$ 5.00\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The five folders cost \\(5\\times\\$2.50=\\$12.50\\). A \\(20\\%\\)-off sale saves \\(20\\%\\) of the original cost. Since \\(20\\%=\\tfrac15\\), Karl could have saved\n\\[\n\\$12.50\\div5=\\boxed{\\$2.50},\n\\]\nchoice C.",
